# Section titles

Every major homepage section uses the shared `SectionHeading` pattern:

- Format: **TITLE · TITLE** (same word twice; first solid accent, second faded)
- Uppercase, bold, teal accent (`text-accent`)
- **No** serial index (`06 —— STACK`, `01`, etc.)
- Parent section width: always `max-w-6xl px-6` so titles align across Work / About / Stack / Commits
- Optional right slot only for badges/controls (e.g. `// PRODUCTION-TESTED`, year tabs)
- Do not wrap `SectionHeading` in a narrower `max-w-*` than the section

```tsx
import { SectionHeading } from "@/components/SectionHeading";

<SectionHeading id="skills-heading" title="Stack" end={/* optional */} />
```

## Examples

| Section | `title` prop |
|---------|----------------|
| About | `About` |
| Experience | `Experience` |
| Skills | `Stack` |
| Commit History | `Commits` |
| Selected Work | `Work` |
| Contact | `Contact` |
| Blog | `Blog` |

## Do not

- Sentence-style or italic gradient section H2s for major sections
- Certifications block on the Skills section (resume/LinkedIn only)
- Hardcoding skills in `SkillsSection` — manage via `/admin/skills` + MongoDB
- Mixing orange nskr colors — use site teal
